  "description": "On a 25-minute clock, run 1.5 miles then use the remaining time for as many rounds as possible of 11 chest-to-bar pull-ups, 7 hang squat cleans and 7 push presses. Honours U.S. Army Capt. Benjamin David Tiffner, killed by an IED in Baghdad in 2007. A fast run buys more rounds, but the barbell work punishes a run you cannot recover from.",
